{"kind":"report","text":"Read-only Judge advisory for immutable aeafd364130fedf937101e2c3e960091b105fd00, tree329b8e934d05c5176755c490ec75daa35b108406, against landed Main698a3d71337a6a03bdea0dfdac10043dd5cbf011.\n\nF1 (medium): preserve actual operation read/page counts when work rejects. In packages/mcp/src/metrics.ts:106 and112, #run initializes or replaces failure numbers with [0,0,0,0]. The accumulated op.reads/op.pages are used only by successful describe callbacks (call:121, list:128). The failure row therefore reports zero attempts and a clean summary after actual reads occurred. A concrete production route is McpService.page(invalidCursor): service.ts:249 first awaits snapshot(), whose configured repository inventory performs session/summary/retained reads; only afterwards does cursor validation throw ListRestart (service.ts:253). The failure classifier emits tools-list/refused/restart, but double5 read attempts is zero. A list transport failure after attempts, or a call/enrol exception after counted reads, has the same defect. This contradicts docs/mcp.md's actual read-attempt map and the commission's operation-owned actual counting requirement.\n\nRepair the kind-specific failure completion mapping using the captured counters: tools-list should retain actual reads in double5; tool-call should retain actual reads/pages in doubles3/4. Zero unavailable result-derived quantities as appropriate. Preserve the original result/exception and nonawaited reporter behavior. Add focused witnesses for an invalid/stale list cursor after real inventory reads and a rejecting operation after observed GET/session/page attempts; check the reported counters as well as exception identity. Existing exception-equivalence tests do not assert these counters. This is a static finding; checker executed no Source, imports, tests, gate or provider request.\n\nCoverage: preparation note read first and in full; every one of the21 changed-path deltas read without unresolved truncation; all six new files read in full (preparation, metrics module/test, evaluator, client, client tests). Existing changed files were inspected by complete deltas plus affected service/list/read/inventory, hosted enrolment, custody transition and Worker wiring contexts. This is not a claim to reread all unchanged lines of the existing files or all Main. Owner test/process evidence in the note remains owner-attributed; no private raw logs or ungranted adjacent evidence were opened.\n\nOther reviewed behavior: multiplicity and sampling applied once per relevant quantity; raw-route weighted nearest-rank p95; 4xx separated from error rate; busy independent of coverage; recorded loss before sampled-unknown; unsampled HTTP place balance uses current create; MCP marker excluded; rows-written remains explicitly unmeasured; bounded SQL/health replies and input files; persisted custody events occur after writes; closed labels and ALS operation isolation. No further concrete defect found in this bounded static pass.\n\nPublic API assumptions were checked against primary Cloudflare documentation only, without account access. The Analytics Engine endpoint, bearer request and _sample_interval model are documented at https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/analytics-engine/sql-api/ . SELECT/LIMIT/FORMAT JSON with data and rows are documented at https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/analytics-engine/sql-reference/statements/ . Wrangler NDJSON session/deploy/version_id and command-failed records are documented at https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/system-environment-variables/ . Those documents do not establish that the project's real SQL, recorded calibration, health or storage-row reader has been accepted; those observations remain owed.\n\nThis is an advisory delivery under31820027/ee8d779a, not a Source verdict. Existing stale commissionbe612eec still needs unchanged-conditions renewal on live f57fc4da/bc00cd27, keeping archive receipt2643d98e historical rather than a freshness basis. Any code repair requires a fresh immutable freeze and its actual composed gate; an earlier standalone gate cannot cover the archive composition. No checker push or deployment/publication action is authorized by this report.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ee8d779a8417d65abdf5c463dab7661f2b30e8c7","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3182002721534b08b9527dc2b3e81d8fc75ce6fa"}}